%I A399885 #12 Nov 10 2026 17:34:18
%S A399885 1,3,14,151,4034,255792,34517966,9475017017,5221073567485,
%T A399885 5761209638019174,12725451428384708284,56252229692306192012486,
%U A399885 497527035055017778587221335,8802996462649354121858945351603,311554682643459341594923783495755712
%N A399885 Number of digraphs on n unlabeled nodes, self-loops disallowed, that are reducible for some election of source-SCC headers.
%C A399885 The unlabeled counterpart of A399554. An election chooses one node in each source strongly connected component (one receiving no edge from outside). Join a new root to these nodes to obtain a flow graph.
%C A399885 A digraph qualifies if some election makes this flow graph reducible in the sense of Hecht and Ullman. Each qualifying digraph is counted once up to isomorphism, not once for each successful election.
%C A399885 Equivalently, every source strongly connected component is reducible from at least one of its nodes, and every non-source component has one node receiving all its incoming edges from other components and is reducible when rooted at that node. All digraphs have no self-loops.
%D A399885 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A399885 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A399885 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A399885 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A399885 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A399885 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A399885/b399885.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..19</a>
%H A399885 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A397968/a397968.py.txt">Required Python module (unlabeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Aug 2026.
%H A399885 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A399885 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A399885 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Required Python module (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%H A399885 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A399885/a399885.py.txt">Python program (unlabeled_reducible_elections.py)</a>, Nov 2026.
%F A399885 a(n) = (1/n!) * Sum_{sigma in S_n} F_some(sigma), where F_some(sigma) is the number of loopless digraphs fixed by sigma that admit at least one reducible election of their source-SCC headers.
%o A399885 (Python)
%o A399885 # Save the five linked Python files in one directory using the filenames
%o A399885 # shown in their link captions, then run Python in that directory.
%o A399885 from unlabeled_reducible_elections import unlabeled_election_sequence
%o A399885 unlabeled_election_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_digraphs_some", 16)
